> basis b1 { cost(x) = ~x }
> basis b2 { gates(x) = ~x }
> basis b3 { lut(x) = ~x }
> basis b4 { and(x, y) = x & y }
> basis b5 { pi(x) = ~x }
> n(a: u1) = ~a
> a2(a: u1, b: u1) = a & b
> gates n basis b1
gates for n: 1 input bit -> 1 output bit, basis b1
  minimal: cost 1, 1 step (no program of cost <= 0 exists; 1 candidates searched)
  checked: the program reproduces every output bit on all 2 care inputs
  t0 = cost(a)                  = ~a
  r0 = t0
> gates n basis b2
gates for n: 1 input bit -> 1 output bit, basis b2
  minimal: cost 1, 1 step (no program of cost <= 0 exists; 1 candidates searched)
  checked: the program reproduces every output bit on all 2 care inputs
  t0 = gates(a)                 = ~a
  r0 = t0
> gates n basis b3
gates for n: 1 input bit -> 1 output bit, basis b3
  minimal: cost 1, 1 step (no program of cost <= 0 exists; 1 candidates searched)
  checked: the program reproduces every output bit on all 2 care inputs
  t0 = lut(a)                   = ~a
  r0 = t0
> gates a2 basis b4
gates for a2: 2 input bits -> 1 output bit, basis b4
  minimal: cost 1, 1 step (no program of cost <= 0 exists; 1 candidates searched)
  checked: the program reproduces every output bit on all 4 care inputs
  t0 = and(a, b)               = a & b
  r0 = t0
> gates n basis b5
gates for n: 1 input bit -> 1 output bit, basis b5
  minimal: cost 1, 1 step (no program of cost <= 0 exists; 1 candidates searched)
  checked: the program reproduces every output bit on all 2 care inputs
  t0 = pi(a)                    = ~a
  r0 = t0
